Before reaching for bigger runners, check what your jobs are actually doing. Ours were mostly waiting on the network.

## Cache the package store

```yaml {% title=".github/workflows/ci.yaml" highlight="9-11" %}
jobs:
  check:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: pnpm/action-setup@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: 22
          cache: pnpm
      - run: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
      - run: pnpm run check
```

## Cache build outputs too

TypeScript's incremental build info is worth caching on its own:

```yaml
- uses: actions/cache@v4
  with:
    path: '**/*.tsbuildinfo'
    key: tsc-${{ hashFiles('**/tsconfig*.json', 'pnpm-lock.yaml') }}
```

{% callout type="danger" title="Never cache secrets" %}
A cache is readable by any workflow on the same branch. Keep `.env` files and credentials out of cached paths.
{% /callout %}
